    group, which recurses once per character. See
    tests/Standards/ComponentMarkupTest.php for the measured thresholds and for
    why the error constant depends on whether the PCRE JIT is on.

    No opening template tag is spelled out anywhere above the corrupted one --
    not even in this comment, which the raw-file precondition in that test reads
    along with everything else. The corrupted wrapper is therefore the first tag
    TEMPLATE_TAG matches, the failed read collects nothing before it gives out,
    and $matches comes back empty.

    The pair below it is correctly wrapped: two adjacent components, each in a
    wrapper of its own carrying the same wire:key the component carries. Read
    normally, the sniff says nothing about them. They are here to pin what a
    failed read does instead -- every wrapper lookup misses against an empty
